# Deployment Architecture

> Note: this project deploys via **Terraform**, not CloudFormation.
> (An earlier version of the diagram overview table in
> `architecture/Readme.md` referenced CloudFormation — that was
> inaccurate for this repo and should be read as Terraform
> throughout.)

## Deployment Model: Validate-Only

This repository is validated, not applied. `terraform init` and
`terraform validate` (and optionally `terraform plan`) are run
against a real AWS provider config; `terraform apply` is deliberately
never run against a live account. See `docs/design-decisions.md` for
why.

## Workflow

1. cd terraform
2. cp terraform.tfvars.example terraform.tfvars
   -> fill in notification_email (required) and anything else you want to override
3. terraform init
   -> downloads the aws (~>5.0) and random (~>3.5) providers
4. terraform validate
   -> confirms the configuration is internally consistent
5. terraform plan
   -> shows what WOULD be created; safe, makes no AWS calls that create resources
6. (not run in this repo) terraform apply

## Ordering / Dependency Graph

Terraform resolves this automatically from resource references, but the logical build order is:

providers.tf
  -> vpc.tf (VPC, subnets, IGW, NAT, route tables)
     -> security-groups.tf (ALB / App / DB SGs, reference VPC + each other)
        -> database.tf (RDS, Secrets Manager — reference DB SG + db subnets)
        -> compute.tf (IAM, launch template, ALB, ASG — reference App/ALB SGs, app subnets, public subnets, and the Secrets Manager secret name for the user-data comment)
           -> monitoring.tf (CloudWatch alarms — reference the ASG and RDS instance created above)

## State

- No remote backend is configured by default — state is local (`terraform.tfstate`, gitignored).
- An S3 + DynamoDB backend block is present but commented out in `terraform/providers.tf`, ready to uncomment once a state bucket and lock table exist. This matters mainly if this project moves from solo/local use to anything collaborative, since local state has no locking and isn't shared.

## What Deploying For Real Would Require

1. Uncomment and configure the `backend "s3"` block, create the bucket + DynamoDB table first (outside Terraform, to avoid a chicken-and-egg problem).
2. Run `terraform apply`, confirm the plan.
3. Confirm the SNS email subscription (link arrives via email).
4. Point real application code / an AMI-baking pipeline at the launch template instead of the placeholder `user_data` bootstrap in `compute.tf`.
5. Add the WAF + HTTPS/ACM + CI/CD pieces listed under the README's Future Improvements — none of which are provisioned in this repo today.

